### Runtime core independent review (IND430)

- Blocking lifecycle race: `RuntimeSupervisor._spawn` checks manager closure before `prepare_launch`, but shutdown snapshots only already registered `_owned_runs` and releases its lifecycle lock without excluding in-flight spawns (`runtime/processes.py:97-117,169-172,339-354`). A barrier-paused preparation followed by shutdown and replacement-manager construction reached instrumented `Popen` with the old manager closed while the replacement held the lock; the admitted run remained RESERVED. Serialize shutdown against spawn/ownership registration or explicitly track and cancel/drain in-flight generations before releasing manager exclusivity. No actual browser was started in this reproduction.
- Blocking recovery findings: `registry.probe_process` returns LIVE for an exact PID/start-time zombie; an actual child left unreaped produced `/proc` state Z and probe LIVE (`runtime/registry.py:47-57`). Treat Z/X as dead so recovery checks the retained browser namespace rather than adopting a dead supervisor. `_process_group_liveness` marks all unreadable `/proc/*/stat` entries uncertain before `_runtime_liveness` reaches its UID filter (`runtime/processes.py:460-488`); a controlled empty-runtime probe with one provably foreign-UID unreadable entry returned UNKNOWN. Ignore provably unrelated foreign-UID entries while retaining uncertainty for same-UID unreadable processes.
- Passed source checks: durable supervisor claim occurs outside confinement before child launch; private boundary namespace is verified and persisted before GO/runner exec; stdout EPIPE retains supervision and restart metadata. Namespace PID/start/executable mapping distinguishes actual browser from boundary. Admission spawns only `newly_reserved`, whole-batch preflight and per-target failures are separate, waits occur outside catalog locking, timeouts retain occupancy, cookie helpers use current scoped authority plus stopped-only ledger admission, and prepare callback runs after authorization/reservation without being used by cookie helpers. Run-qualified CAS and verified group signaling protect replacements. Public DTOs omit private runtime fields. No simplification-only change warranted.
- Verification: shared baseline Python, focused `tests/test_ext_runtime.py tests/test_ext_supervisor.py tests/test_ext_storage.py`: **38 passed**; Ruff on eight scoped implementation files and three test files: **passed**. Three additional read-only reproductions above expose uncovered blockers. No source/test edits or branch/index/commit/push operations by this review.
- Limits: cache/confinement/upstream-hook source review belongs to peer reviewer; real-bubblewrap stand-in test was included, but actual Camoufox/Xvfb, browser proxy/WebRTC/persistence/geometry, noVNC, ARM64 and target-host acceptance remain NOT RUN. Integration must supply fresh personal-session/ACL authorization and shared catalog locking for every effect; this review does not establish complete slice 9.


